keeping the arts alive here in las vegas  the pandemic has left many entertainers  struggling to stay afloat  so a special benefit was held tonight to  help them bounce back  madison kimbrough attended that welcome  back vegas event tonight she joins us  live from stoney's rock and country with  the latest  madison yeah sasha people got the  opportunity to watch these las vegas  entertainers perform  once again live for free as you can see  we're right here at stoney's rockin  country bar  this was an event meant to help  struggling las vegas artists bounce back  and book gigs once again take a look  with the entertainment industry taking  one of the biggest hits during the  pandemic  those in the performing arts need our  support more than ever  they are born entertainers that's what  they do they  that's their life that's their  livelihood  marty b who is no stranger to the  entertainment world of las vegas  worked decades in the trade show  industry and he knew he had to do  something for his  fellow entertainment performers it was  heartbreaking to see people entertaining  each other because they couldn't  entertain on stage  saturday night marty b's save our arts  foundation hosted welcome back las vegas  a live benefit concert  with the goal to raise money for these  struggling artists from comedy to  musical performances  artists shared how this year has  impacted them the last year has been  scary to go from nine shows a week  between my show  and the band to none to them maybe three  is you know it hurts your soul  especially as a performer  it's not just work for us we love what  we do it's been tough  it's been a struggle really hard but at  the same time you know it's  you just have to hang in there you know  whatever you know we're basically  gypsies  so we have to make it up as we go the  hope is that this event will be the  first of many  targeting those in the performing arts  industry and helping them get back on  their feet  and the welcome back vegas event is also  available on pay-per-view with the  proceeds going directly to the artist  tonight's admission was free and the  event lasted for about three hours  reporting live madison kimbrough 8 news  now
 

